# IMPLEMENTATION_STEPS: cu-005

1. Verify the infrastructure without provisioning it. Run:

```sh
./scripts/newspipe status
```

Do NOT touch: pipelines/**, conf/ingestion.conf, conf/feeds.conf

Prove: `./scripts/newspipe status | head -1`

Stop when the first line reads `infra present: kafka, rustfs, opencode`. If it does not, report BLOCKED and do not run `./scripts/newspipe up`.

2. Back up the operator file and set the E2E overrides. The tracked default stays in conf/enrichment.conf; this step changes only the ignored .env:

```sh
cp .env /tmp/newspipe.env.bak
python3 - <<'PY'
from pathlib import Path
p = Path(".env")
lines = [l for l in p.read_text().splitlines()
         if not l.startswith("NEWSPIPE_OPENCODE_MODEL=")
         and not l.startswith("NEWSPIPE_OPENCODE_FALLBACK_MODELS=")
         and not l.startswith("NEWSPIPE_POLL_INTERVAL_SECONDS=")]
lines += [
    "NEWSPIPE_OPENCODE_MODEL=nvidia/nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning-30b-a3b",
    "NEWSPIPE_OPENCODE_FALLBACK_MODELS=nvidia/poolside/laguna-xs-2.1",
    "NEWSPIPE_POLL_INTERVAL_SECONDS=60",
]
p.write_text("\n".join(lines) + "\n")
PY
```

Do NOT touch: conf/enrichment.conf, pipelines/ingestion/**, conf/feeds.conf

Prove: `grep -E 'NEWSPIPE_OPENCODE_(MODEL|FALLBACK_MODELS)' .env`

Stop when the proof prints the nvidia primary and the nvidia fallback.

3. Start the enrichment pipeline through scripts/newspipe and wait for one poll line with a non-zero enriched count and zero failures:

```sh
timeout 300 ./scripts/newspipe run enrichment > /tmp/enrich-e2e.log 2>&1 &
for i in $(seq 1 120); do grep -q 'poll merged' /tmp/enrich-e2e.log && break; sleep 2; done
grep -E 'poll merged [0-9]+ enriched units \([1-9][0-9]* enriched, 0 failed\)' /tmp/enrich-e2e.log
```

Do NOT touch: pipelines/ingestion/**, conf/enrichment.conf, conf/feeds.conf

Prove: `grep -E 'poll merged [0-9]+ enriched units \([1-9][0-9]* enriched, 0 failed\)' /tmp/enrich-e2e.log`

Stop when the proof prints exactly one or more matching lines and no `startup aborted` line exists.

4. Stop the pipeline and confirm the consumer group committed a non-zero offset:

```sh
./scripts/newspipe down
docker exec kafka /opt/kafka/bin/kafka-consumer-groups.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --describe --group enrichment-group | awk '$1 == "enrichment-group" && $2 == "raw_rss" { if ($4 > 0) found = 1 } END { exit !found }'
```

Do NOT touch: pipelines/ingestion/**, conf/enrichment.conf, conf/feeds.conf

Prove: `./scripts/newspipe status | grep 'enrichment-group'`

Stop when the docker awk command exits 0 and the status line shows a committed offset above zero.

5. Restore the operator .env and confirm no timeout was logged:

```sh
cp /tmp/newspipe.env.bak .env
rm /tmp/newspipe.env.bak
grep -c 'opencode run timed out' /tmp/enrich-e2e.log
```

Do NOT touch: conf/enrichment.conf, pipelines/ingestion/**, conf/feeds.conf

Prove: `grep -c 'opencode run timed out' /tmp/enrich-e2e.log`

Stop when the proof prints 0, the .env file is restored, and `git status --short pipelines conf` is empty.
